  "raw_text": "The two backup drives were named \"inference_1\" and \"inference_2\" rather than \"backup1\" and \"backup2\" or \"tension1\" and \"tension2.\" The word \"tension\" was rejected because it is an overloaded LLM term, carrying unwanted word-association baggage from model outputs. The underscore separator was chosen over no separator because the digit 1 and lowercase letter L are visually indistinguishable in many terminal fonts, making \"inference1\" ambiguous at a glance. The underscore convention also aligns with the project's existing naming standard for files and directories.",
